# id: BM97-cover-skips-the-level-one-file
# blinds: L1 being asked whether it holds a covering tombstone
# covering-lane: cpp-test
# expect: killed
# control-lane: cpp-build
# expect-control: alive
#
# BM96 one level down, and the one that only appears after a compaction has run.
# A range delete survives the flush, survives every read while its table is in
# L0, and stops the moment a compaction moves it to L1 -- so the failure is
# separated from the write by an arbitrary amount of time and by an operation
# the caller never asked for.
